// Title: Suspicious Curl Change User Agents - Linux
// Sigma ID: b86d356d-6093-443d-971c-9b07db583c68
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1071.001
// Description: Detects a suspicious curl process start on linux with set useragent options
// False positives:
//   - Scripts created by developers and admins
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://curl.se/docs/manpage.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_susp_curl_useragent.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/curl" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -A " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --user-agent ")
